    },
    {
      "id": "850dfc2c26c9c43f7d4ec777cf92cdb77d68f88d",
      "short_id": "850dfc2c",
      "created_at": "2020-09-16T12:09:20.000+02:00",
      "parent_ids": [
        "d02ddfb9b1e1106dd2d585a6ee4a10f01ed28bb7"
      ],
      "title": "afs: use a simpler way to read a time field",
      "message": "afs: use a simpler way to read a time field\n\nIf a time field uses a standard enconding, we can call proto_tree_add_item()\nto add it to the tree. There's no need to parse the time field ourselves.\n\nUpdate two places in the afs dissector where the manual parsing can\neasily be replaced with a proto_tree_add_item() call.\n",
      "author_name": "Martin Kaiser",
      "author_email": "wireshark@kaiser.cx",
      "authored_date": "2020-09-14T11:24:02.000+02:00",
      "committer_name": "Martin Kaiser",
